From 13b8199f0a47a3874366f884c7255562141dad19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lu Jialin <lujialin4@huawei.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Oct 2022 19:47:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 0904/1076] [Huawei] cgroup: support cgroup writeback on
 cgroupv1

Offering: HULK
hulkl inclusion
category: feature
bugzilla: 187773

-------------------------------

In cgroupv1, cgroup writeback is not supproted for two problems:
1) Blkcg_css and memcg_css are mounted on different cgroup trees.
   Therefore, blkcg_css cannot be found according to a certain memcg_css.
2) Buffer I/O is worked by kthread, which is in the root_blkcg.
   Therefore, blkcg cannot limit wbps and wiops of buffer I/O.

We solve the two problems to support cgroup writeback on cgroupv1.
1) Blkcg_root_css is attached to a memcg when is was created.
2) We add a number "wb_blkio_ino" in mem_cgroup_legacy_files.
   User can attach a blkcg_css to a memcg through echo the file
   inode of the blkcg into the wb_blkio of the memcg.
3) inode_cgwb_enabled() return true when memcg and io are mounted on
   cgroupv2 or cgroupv1.
4) Buffer I/O can find a blkcg according to its page's memcg.

Thus, a memcg can find a certain blkcg, and cgroup writeback can be
supported on cgroupv1.

Signed-off-by: Lu Jialin <lujialin4@huawei.com>
